\description{
Compute response means, variances and descriptive Infit/Outfit summaries.
Ordinary and extended RSMs and two-family GPCMs integrate uncertain latent effects; corrected
GPCM JML conditions on saved calibration and reprofiled Person estimates.
}
\details{
Holding calibration \eqn{\widehat\psi} fixed, posterior routes evaluate
\deqn{p_{ik}=E[P(Y_i^{rep}=k\mid b,\widehat\psi)\mid Y_{obs},\widehat\psi], \qquad \mu_i=\sum_k k p_{ik},\quad V_i=\sum_k (k-\mu_i)^2p_{ik},}
integrating uncertain latent effects \eqn{b} across all observed ratings of
the Person (quadrature for ordinary RSM and two-family GPCM; nested
quadrature for testlets; category-specific Laplace numerator integrals with
\code{NormalizationError} for shared random raters). Profile-score-adjusted GPCM
JML instead evaluates conditional plug-in probabilities
\eqn{p_{ik}=P(Y_i=k\mid\widehat\theta_i,\widehat\beta_{adj})} without
quadrature; extreme profiles have \code{Status = "zero_variance"} and
\code{StandardizedResidual = NA} (\code{0/0} is never replaced with zero, so Infit can
remain available when total group variance is positive while Outfit becomes
\code{NA} / \code{partially_available}).

Grouped descriptive Outfit (mean of \eqn{(y_i-\mu_i)^2/V_i}) and Infit
(\eqn{\sum_i(y_i-\mu_i)^2/\sum_i V_i}) have no expectation-one baseline, ZSTD,
or automatic cutoffs, and any unresolved row withholds that group's summary.

\code{plot()} method: Plot descriptive response residual summaries

Compare residual summaries across selected groups without reference cutoffs.

For \code{plot()}: The response probabilities integrate the latent effects conditional
on the same observed responses and fixed calibration. These are descriptive
summaries, not ordinary plug-in Infit/Outfit. Neither an expectation of
one nor a universal acceptable range is established. No interval, warning
region or statistical test is drawn. Hiding annotations changes only the
display; \code{\link[=plot_data]{plot_data()}} retains the probability definition and limitations.
For corrected JML, probabilities instead condition on corrected calibration
and reprofiled Person point estimates; no latent effects are integrated.
The paired view displays each available index independently, so an
available Infit is retained when zero conditional variance makes Outfit
undefined. The scatter view requires both indices. The caption reports
partial availability, and the saved table retains its reasons.
}
